# Fault injection, testing=UnderstateEffects:Builtin/String.prototype.toUpperCase/KindOfResult: the signature of String.prototype.toUpperCase declares null as its only result.
# A type that is a single marker (null, undefined) needs no register, so the operation of the inline code (CallInline) held no value, and the check that runs on each operation skipped it.
# `typeof` was folded to "object" at compile time, and the call, which had no user left, was removed.
# The program printed "object" instead of "string" and did not crash, even with testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime.
# Now, with that switch, such an operation keeps the result of the inline code, and the result is checked.
